/*  A kij FROM GROUPS, AT A DECLARED TEMPERATURE.  A cubic needs one binary
    correction kij per pair, and a measured one exists for few pairs.  PPR78
    (Jaubert & Mutelet) predicts it from the GROUPS each molecule is made of:

        k_ij(T) = [ E_ij(T) - (delta_i - delta_j)^2 ] / ( 2 delta_i delta_j )
        delta_i = sqrt(a_i(T)) / b_i                (Choupo's own PR78)
        E_ij(T) = -1/2 SUM_k SUM_l (alpha_ik - alpha_jk)(alpha_il - alpha_jl)
                       A_kl (298.15 / T)^(B_kl / A_kl - 1)

    so kij DEPENDS ON T.  The `ppr78Kij` op evaluates it ONCE, at the
    temperature it is told, and writes the matrix to a FILE -- a kij SET
    record (`recordType eosBinaryInteractionSet;`) that a phi-phi package
    then declares -- with the three terms of the quotient beside every
    value, so the division can be redone by hand.

    WHAT THIS CASE SHOWS.  The same three pairs at two temperatures:
      * 280 K: every pair (CH4-CO2, CH4-H2, CO2-H2) lies inside the T range
        of the binary data its group parameters were fitted on (Xu et al.
        2017, Table 2) -- nothing is marked;
      * 500 K: every pair lies above that range, and the set writes
        `extrapolated yes;` with the window on each of them.
    The components are each their own group, so alpha is 1 or 0 and E_ij
    is the single group-pair term.

    THE GROUP TABLE is constant/parameters/PPR78/xu2017.dat, the E-PPR78
    subset (Xu, Lasala, Privat & Jaubert, Int. J. Greenh. Gas Control 56
    (2017) 126-154, Table 3); its own header explains its transcription
    and that it is `reviewStatus interim`.

    WHAT IS NOT VALIDATED.  Nothing here is compared with a measurement:
    the numbers are Eq. 4 evaluated on the cited table and the engine's own
    PR78 a_i(T), b_i.  Whether those kij reproduce a phase diagram is not
    asked here.

    THE TWO SET FILES are run outputs: they carry the date they were
    written, so they are named `*.proposal.dat`, which git ignores.
*/

operations
(
    {
        name        kij_280K;
        type        ppr78Kij;
        groupTable  "constant/parameters/PPR78/xu2017.dat";
        T           280 K;
        components  ( CH4 CO2 H2 );
        output      { record "constant/parameters/PengRobinson/ppr78_280K.proposal.dat"; }
    }
    {
        name        kij_500K;
        type        ppr78Kij;
        groupTable  "constant/parameters/PPR78/xu2017.dat";
        T           500 K;
        components  ( CH4 CO2 H2 );
        output      { record "constant/parameters/PengRobinson/ppr78_500K.proposal.dat"; }
    }
);
